MathCAT (braille, Nemeth and UEB): official signs the tables lacked

Mathessible sent every character of the maths blocks through MathCAT and
looked each one missing up in the codes' own references. Most have no
official sign at all (Nemeth and UEB both say to use a transcriber-defined
symbol with a note), and MathCAT's hex code stays for them. These do:

Nemeth (Nemeth Code 2022, Appendix D, Index of Nemeth Braille Symbols):
- ⩽ ⩾ ⪕ ⪖ ⪛ ⪜ ⫹ ⫺: listed as print variants of ≤ ≥ ⋜ ⋝ ⪙ ⪚ ≦ ≧
  ("≤ or ⩽"), so they take the same signs.
- ˹ ˺ ˻ ˼ and ⎡ ⎤ ⎣ ⎦: the upper and lower half brackets (19.4,
  "⎡ or ˹"), ⠈⠘⠷ ⠈⠘⠾ ⠈⠰⠷ ⠈⠰⠾.
- ◺ right triangle ⠫⠞⠨⠗⠻, ⏢ trapezoid ⠫⠵, ◼ filled-in square ⠫⠸⠲,
  ℞ crossed R ⠈⠠⠗.

UEB:
- ⦀ triple vertical bar ⠼⠸⠇ (Rules of Unified English Braille 2024,
  Appendix 3, Symbols List).
- ⦜ measured right angle ⠼⠸⠪ (UEB Guidelines for Technical Material,
  2014, section 11).

Kept at the end of each file, away from patch 0006's lines, so both
still apply and check on their own. Applied by scripts/bootstrap.sh on
top of upstream 85c89a37. Worth proposing upstream to daisy/MathCAT.

